# Codebase Engineer — frontend build-time environment variables
#
# Unlike backend/.env.example, these are Vite build-time variables — they
# get baked into the built JS bundle when you run `npm run build` (or the
# Docker image build, via deploy/Dockerfile's `ARG`/`ENV` — see
# deploy/docker-compose.yml's `build.args`). Setting one after the app is
# already built has no effect; you have to rebuild.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in this directory for local `npm run dev`/`npm
# run build`. `.env` is gitignored — real values never get committed.

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key (the PUBLIC half of the pair — the secret
# key stays server-side as backend/.env's TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY). This one
# is meant to be embedded in the page the browser loads. Leave unset and
# the widget renders nothing at all — bot protection stays fully opt-in,
# matching docs/AUTH.md §4.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
